WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.083
Detection engineering succeeds through collaboration.

2
00:00:03.083 --> 00:00:14.049
SOC analysts provide insight into alert quality, investigation workflows, escalation paths, and operational realities that may not be obvious from the logic alone.

3
00:00:14.049 --> 00:00:20.554
Threat hunters can identify gaps, test hypotheses, and reveal emerging opportunities for detection.

4
00:00:20.554 --> 00:00:27.848
Incident responders contribute lessons learned from investigations, including which signals helped and which context was missing.

5
00:00:27.848 --> 00:00:32.118
Strong feedback loops improve both detections and defensive outcomes.

6
00:00:32.118 --> 00:00:41.567
When analysts can report noise, ambiguity, missing fields, or useful context, detection engineers can make practical improvements that reduce friction.

7
00:00:41.567 --> 00:00:45.359
Collaboration also improves documentation and usability.

8
00:00:45.359 --> 00:00:54.379
A detection should help the person receiving it understand what happened, why it matters, and what reasonable next steps might be in the organizationâ€™s workflow.
